    70	## 1. The claim to be proved, stated with all quantifiers
    71	
    72	Throughout, a **row-`(d,n)` member** is a pair `(D, ν)` where `ν : A^1 → A^2`, `t ↦ (P(t),Q(t))`,
    73	is a polynomial map that is **birational onto its image** `D`, with `deg_t P = d`, `deg_t Q = n`,
    74	`d > n`. Such a `D` automatically has exactly one place at infinity. Write
    75	
    76	* `A_D := C[P,Q] ⊂ C[t]` — the affine coordinate ring of `D` (`ν` birational ⇒ `A_D` has fraction
    77	  field `C(t)` and `C[t]` is its integral closure);
    78	* `v := deg_t`, and `S_D := v(A_D \ {0}) ⊆ N` — the **semigroup at infinity** of `D` in the sense
    79	  of `GM` Definition 2.2 (`S_{C,∞} = {−ν_{C,p}(h) : h ∈ O_C(C∖{p})}`; for a polynomial
    80	  parametrisation `−ν_{C,p}(h) = deg_t h(P,Q)`);
    81	* `δ_aff(D) := Σ_{p ∈ D} δ_p = dim_C C[t]/A_D`, the affine double-point number;
    82	* `Δ = (δ_0, …, δ_g)` — the Abhyankar–Moh δ-sequence of `D`, which by `GM` Theorem 2.1
    83	  **generates** `S_D` and satisfies axioms (1)–(3) there.
    84	
    85	The explicit families of the promoted theorem (`CI5` §1) are, for `b ∈ C`, `c ∈ C^*`,
    86	
    87	```text
    88	  r = t^3 + b t + c ,      q = t^4 + (2b/3) t^2 + (4c/3) t ,
    89	  D_{b,c}  = image of  t ↦ ( r(t)^2 , q(t) ) ,
    90	  D'_{b,c} = image of  t ↦ ( r(t)^2 + q(t)^2 , q(t) )  =  Φ^{-1}(D_{b,c}),   Φ(x,y) = (x−y^2, y).
    91	```
    92	
    93	> **THEOREM EXHAUST.** *Let `(D,ν)` be a member of the campaign's N=4 residual curve rows, i.e.*
    94	>
    95	> * *(i) a row-`(6,4)` member with `Δ = (6,4,3)`, or*
