3.1. Generalities on plane valuations. To begin with, we recall the general concept
of valuation.
Definition 3.1. A valuation of a field K is a mapping
                                     ν : K ∗ (:= K \ {0}) → G,
where G is a totally ordered group, such that it satisfies
      • ν(f + g) ≥ min{ν(f ), ν(g)} and
      • ν(f g) = ν(f ) + ν(g),
f, g being elements in K ∗ . The subring of K, Rν := {f ∈ K ∗ |ν(f ) ≥ 0} ∪ {0}, is called
the valuation ring of ν. Rν is a local ring whose maximal ideal is mν := {f ∈ K ∗ |ν(f ) >
0} ∪ {0}.
