    93	## 5. Part B — EDGE-MODULI: singularity typing at j=-27/4 and j=-81/16
    94	
    95	ROW-NF (`EM` from `ZVK:154-163`, not re-proved here): `x=r(t)^2`, `y=q(t)`, `r=t^3+bt+c`, `q=t^4+(2b/3)t^2+(4c/3)t`, `c≠0`, `j=b^3/c^2`. Plus-branch coincidences are the roots of `h(e)=e^3+(4b/3)e-4c/3`, with `p=ts=e^2+b`. The minus branch is empty for `c≠0` (consumed). Discriminants: `disc(r)=0 ⇔ j=-27/4` and `disc(h)=0 ⇔ j=-81/16` are elementary in `j` (`-4b^3-27c^2` and the cubic discriminant of `h`, the latter reducing to `j=-81/16`).
